      "instruction": "You are shown the documented rules of the checks, not their code. Write ONE test pair: an input and your own rewritten version of it, and say what the RULE, read as written, says the check's answer ought to do: move ('moves') or stay ('unchanged'). Your expectation comes from the rule's words alone. Aim for the cases the wording leaves open or decides by a clause a reader could miss: what counts as inside a fence, what counts as top-level, what prose around or inside a fence does, what a second object does, what the refusal list's order does. Your kernel is one of conformance.kernel.recovery, conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose, conformance.kernel.response-verdict, and your input is a reply: a JSON object alone or with prose or fences around it. The commitments are a STRING whose content is JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"input\": \"<the input text>\", \"rewritten\": \"<your rewritten text>\", \"expect\": \"moves\" or \"unchanged\", \"rewrite\": \"<one sentence naming what you changed>\"}. The input and the rewritten text are instances written out in full, never descriptions. Do not repeat a pair shown among the earlier proposals.",
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "kernel",
                  "input",
                  "rewritten",
                  "expect",
                  "rewrite"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "kernel": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^conformance\\.kernel\\.(recovery|recovered-from-prose|response-verdict)$"
                  },
                  "input": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "rewritten": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "expect": {
                    "enum": [
                      "moves",
                      "unchanged"
                    ]
                  },
                  "rewrite": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 3
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "commitment_call": "single"
    },
