      "instruction": "You are shown the documented rules of the checks, not their code. Write ONE test pair: an input and your own rewritten version of it, and say what the RULE, read as written, says the check's answer ought to do: move ('moves') or stay ('unchanged'). Your expectation comes from the rule's words alone. Aim for the cases the wording leaves open or decides by a clause a reader could miss: what counts as inside a fence, what counts as top-level, what prose around or inside a fence does, what a second object does, what the refusal list's order does. Your kernel is conformance.kernel.refusal-phrase or conformance.kernel.response-verdict, and your input is a reply in prose, with or without a JSON object. The commitments are a STRING whose content is JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"input\": \"<the input text>\", \"rewritten\": \"<your rewritten text>\", \"expect\": \"moves\" or \"unchanged\", \"rewrite\": \"<one sentence naming what you changed>\"}. The input and the rewritten text are instances written out in full, never descriptions. Do not repeat a pair shown among the earlier proposals.",
